d nobody knows their name and that's  very very wrong  because they should have had a gold as  well obviously i mean what would it what  difference would it have made to you  having your gold and not a silver  um if there's a big difference isn't  there between being an olympics of  adolescent being an olympic champion um  it would have been lovely you know at  times it would great if i was away at  the olympics i remember  when becky amazingly won her two golds  in beijing back in 2008 and everyone was  very excited and they constantly  referred to the last time a british girl  won a medal which was in the 60s you  know won a championships and that was  hard to deal with when we knew  categorically what was going on you know  we had all the stasi evidence we knew  exactly what they were taking when they  were taking it  so i think  i'm the last person to say that i want  anyone to turn up on anyone's door and  take their medals away i think what  should happen now is that the record  books should be changed and that new  medals maybe should be issued but  those girls were also victims of the  system and that needs to be acknowledged  and it never needs to happen again  and looking at the reasons why why it  was happening or why why it wasn't  tackled i mean it wasn't just because  people didn't want to go back to those  cold war times and it was something that  happened in the past and they just  didn't want to talk about it or was it  something do you think fundamentally  wrong with the governing body of  swimming  um not just swimming you know it wasn't  just something swimming was one of the  worst sports affected but also it  happened a lot in track and field it  happened in rowing you know the great  kathy cook was one of the most amazing  british athletes ever um she held the  400 meter record up until recently when  christina horague beat it and yet most  people again do not know who kathy cook  is so it's by far not just a swimming  problem but i'm very proud that fina the  swimming body now are the first to  actually say we want to do syria  something serious about this it was  endemic  they had east german doctors sitting on  the international ilc olympic doping  panel which is ridiculous and in fact  they even have awards still in place for  people that were given a criminal record  after the war came down who forced these  young girls to take these terrible drugs  so something has to be done to remove  those people and acknowledge what  actually happened  you talked about the girls and the  terrible legacy it has had on them um  how are many of them managing because i  i imagine that you you still have  contact with with these people that you  spent time with when you were younger  yeah not too much contact a little bit i  did a documentary um in 1990 when i met  petra um she was quite poorly then she  was only quite young i remember i took  my little girl with me who was three  months old and that was great and she's  now 23  and she got very upset because she  couldn't have any more children and she  was already on heart pills in fact we've  seen a few of the east german females  actually die since then so you know it's  it was very dire what actually happened  and i'm hoping that finna will will  clear the whole house up you know we've  unfortunately had a president in place  who wasn't always looking at putting the  athletes first and center which is  what's most important it was often about  what's the best hotel they can stay in  how much money can the association make  and sport has to be about the athletes  and it would be really wonderful to see  that this has been sorted out and it  would give the right message that  cheating with drugs or any form of  cheating is not to be accepted and when  they find out they will do something  about it  in terms of the people that were  affected it was as you say it was the  the women that um  took these drugs and they were the ones  that that had all of these success